Hooray!

My second ascention (and first for v3.4.3).  I had nearly ascended a
wizard a few weeks ago, but for an unfortunate accident involving a pit
outside of the sanctum and a wielded cockatrice corpse (I won't be
making that mistake again).

I had a very lucky start with dl3 having a huge hardware store that
included a magic lamp, bag of holding and a magic marker.

I decided to do the gnomish mines first and made my way down to
minetown.  On the way down I found another magic marker, I think I
ended up with about 5 or 6 by the end of the game.

I was browsing through one of the shops and found two small mimics.  I
was worried that I was bound for YASD, so started reading my
unidentified scrolls in the hope of finding a solution.  Luckily the
last scroll I read was an uncursed scroll of genocide and I was able to
wipe out all small mimics.

I had found and identified a luckstone from a bones file using the
naming trick, so there wasn't really much point in going to the bottom
of mines.  Instead I went back to the main branch.  The encounter with
the mimics had scared me, so I decided that +2 silver dragon scale mail
was much more important than a permanent light source.

On level 5, I converted an altar and sacrificed for a while until I got
magicbane.  Since I already had both reflection and a bag of holding,
Sokoban didn't hold much appeal and it too was skipped.

I'm still buzzing from ascending, so I'll just give some quick notes to
the rest of the game instead of a long and boring story that nobody is
really interested in.

There were a couple of firsts in this game.
* First time visiting Fort Ludios
* First time I had a wish from a smoky potion (full healing)
* First time I carried around a stack of meatballs to nullify all cats
and dogs.
* First time I was double troubled.
* First time I used and broke a wand of teleport to clear my path on
the Astral plane.

At one point I had a chameleon, 2 cats, a dog and a pony as pets, but
no magic whistle, so they got left behind if they were too slow
following me to the down stairs.

I didn't get fire resistance until DL39 when a hell hound corpse
finally gave me what I needed.

